course: dictionary
lesson: 3121
title: Words for people's jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a job. An electrician is a person whose job is to put in, check and repair electrical wires, sockets, lights and machines. You will meet phrases like «call an electrician» and «a qualified electrician».
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Wiring must be done by a trained electrician, because mistakes with electricity can cause fires and shocks.» The words trained, fires and shocks tell you this job is serious and needs training. Swap in your meaning: "Wiring must be done by a person whose job is to put in and repair wires" still makes sense.
explain: Context also tells you what you should not do yourself. «Only adults reset a trip, and if it keeps tripping, an electrician checks it.» If a trip keeps happening, you do not fix it yourself. You tell an adult, and an electrician checks it.
fact: An electrician's job is to put in, check and repair electrical wires, sockets, lights and machines.
fact: «Electrician» is a noun, and its plural is «electricians».
fact: «Wiring must be done by a trained electrician.» Never poke anything into a socket.
fact: The ending -cian is used for people's jobs from words ending in c: musician, magician, electrician.
fact: An architect designs a building, and builders, electricians and plumbers help build it.
exercise: What is an electrician? | A person who sells sweets in a shop | A person who drives a bus | A person who grows vegetables on a farm | *A person whose job is to put in, check and repair electrical wires, sockets and lights
exercise: «Only adults reset a trip, and if it keeps tripping, an electrician checks it.» Who checks a trip that keeps happening? | *An electrician | A child with a torch | A visitor who is passing by | The family cat
exercise: Which word follows the same -cian pattern as electrician? | *musician | teacher | singer | driver
test: «Mistakes with electricity can cause fires and shocks.» Why must wiring be done by a trained electrician? | Because wiring is always blue | *Because mistakes with electricity can be dangerous | Because electricians are the tallest people | Because wires are very cheap
test: «An architect designs a building and works with engineers; builders, electricians, plumbers and many others build it.» Who helps build the building? | Nobody, it builds itself | Only the architect | The engineers alone | *Builders, electricians, plumbers and many others
exam: If a plug is scorched, what should you do? | *Tell an adult or call an electrician | Poke it with a knife to see inside | Keep using it, it is probably fine | Dip it in a bucket of water
